## F. FINA 405 project specification (`01_Brief/FINA405_Project_v3.md`) — what each section requires
| ID | Requirement | Exact text / formula |
|---|---|---|
| P01 | Role & teams | CFO of a US-listed multinational evaluating expansion; teams of 3 USD + 3 TEC (cover of Team 9 lists 4+3) |
| P02 | Global assumptions | No credit risk; firm borrows/lends at risk-free (government) spot rates; **all rates annual with semiannual compounding**; market data per country provided later; live scenario in final presentation; research must be cited |
| P03 | §1 Company | Business overview; 3 years audited financials (Yahoo/Bloomberg): growth, margins, Debt/Equity, Net debt/EBITDA, share of revenues and costs in local currency; **≥ 5 ratios vs peers**; market share + **3–5 competitors**; industry overview (growth, cyclicality, capital intensity, regulation); FX (net payer/receiver), interest-rate, inflation risks linked to §3–7 |
| P04 | §2 Country | Inflation + central-bank target; exchange-rate regime; interest-rate structure (short vs long); political/sovereign risk; 5-year forward-looking risks |
| P05 | §3 FRA | (a) payment 1–2 yrs from now; (b) receipt 3–5 yrs from now; Scenario-0 curve → **12×24 FRA and 36×60 FRA**; show accumulation factors (semiannual); interpret as borrowing cost / lending return / hedged exposure and vs spot |
| P06 | §4 Bond | **5-year fixed-rate bond, local currency, face value = USD 100M converted at Scenario-0 spot, 4% annual coupon paid semiannually**; (a) fair value by discounting semiannual flows at local yields; (b) YTM implied by market pricing |
| P07 | §5 Forwards | IRP: **F_t = S₀ × (1 + i_quote/2)^{2t} / (1 + i_base/2)^{2t}** with F_t = local currency per USD, i_quote = domestic, i_base = US; t = 0.5, 1.0, … **5.0**; (a) hedge coupons and principal to lock USD value; (b) mechanics; (c) advantages/limitations vs **options and money-market hedges** |
| P08 | §6 IRS | Expect declining rates; swap structure (notional, fixed paid, floating received e.g. TIIE 6M / EURIBOR 6M, maturity, frequency vs coupon); effective cost of debt after swap with both legs; **IRS contract is in the Excel file (not provided yet)** |
| P09 | Assignment — Kuwait | Group 9: Kuwait, KWD, Halliburton (HAL): "Major oilfield services contracts with Kuwait Oil Company (KOC); **KWD/USD peg makes interest rate risk the primary concern**" |
| P10 | §7 New conditions | Scenario 1Y (provided later): FX update, new curve, FRA 12×24 profit/loss, new forwards 0.5…4.0 yrs, hedge performance |
| P11 | §8 Recommendation | (a) table of 3 strategies: unhedged fixed bond, fixed bond + FX forward, floating bond after IRS — all-in USD cost, risks retained, hedging effectiveness; (b) 2–3 paragraph recommendation linked to §1, §2 and §3–7 |
| P12 | Consequence for the deck | The KWD exposure in §4–5 exists **by construction** (the bond is issued in KWD against a USD functional currency) — it does not depend on whether KOC contracts are KWD-denominated (H22); KWD receipts only matter as a *natural hedge* |

